      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:mhd_generator",
      "title": "MHD Generator",
      "text": "A conducting fluid driven through a magnetic field makes current with no moving parts: the flow itself is the armature.$(br2)Generates power.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Burns a conducting fluid: $(item)Deep Brine$(), $(item)Basaltic Magma$() or $(item)Stellar Plasma$(). Power per volume is \u03c3u\u00b2B\u00b2k(1 \u2212 k): more field and more speed give more, the load factor k is best at one half - unless the current density would arc the electrodes away."
    },
